<rml>
<head>
    <title>VIXEN Editor</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="editor.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
    <div data-model="editor_layers" id="panel">
        <div class="title">Layers</div>
        <!-- Inc-A2 (View-Model-Binding-Inc-A2-Plan-2026-07.md): layer rows are now data-model-bound,
             replacing the Inc1 static markup (3 hand-authored "checkbox checked" divs). Each row's
             id (row.elementId, "layer-<index>-toggle" -- built once in EditorLayersView::
             PopulateFromMask, not re-derived here via string concat) still carries hit-mask="none"
             so UISelectionProviderNode's click hit-test resolves it and EditorApplication::Update
             drains the id via DrainClickedElementId and dispatches it through AppFlowRuntime::
             DispatchBySelector (Inc-4 reframe R5 — the editor names no action verbs). row.isChecked
             drives the "checked" class the same way hud.rml's data-class-focused et al. do. -->
        <div class="row" data-for="row : layers">
            <div data-attr-id="row.elementId" class="checkbox" data-class-checked="row.isChecked" hit-mask="none"></div>
            <span class="col-name">{{row.name}}</span>
            <span class="col-op">{{row.op}}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="hint">Click a box to toggle a layer. Press S to save.</div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
